.TH EUCLID-CLI-EDS-GET-ANSWER 1 "November 2026" "euclid-cli 2.3.2" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eds-get-answer \- show what the name server answers for a name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eds get-answer
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
[\fB\-\-type\fR|\fB\-t\fR \fITYPE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Asks the name server a question and shows its answer \- the same one a
DNS client gets from the DNS port, without needing a DNS client, the
port being reachable, or the local resolver being set up to send the
name there.
.PP
It answers from every zone the server holds, including
.I euclid.internal
and other accounts' zones, since that is what the DNS port does too.
No grant on a zone is needed to see it.
.PP
A name in none of the zones is shown as
.B REFUSED
and not authoritative. The DNS port would forward that name upstream
instead, if forwarders are configured and the client may recurse; this
command never forwards.
.PP
The answer comes from what the server currently has loaded. A record
written a moment ago on another instance may not be in it for up to
the refresh interval.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
The name to look up. Required.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-type " " \fITYPE\fR
The record type to ask for: any stored type, or
.BR SOA ,
.B NS
or
.BR ANY .
Defaults to
.BR A .
.SH OUTPUT
A JSON object:
.TP
.I rcode
.B NOERROR
\- the name exists, with or without records of that type;
.B NXDOMAIN
\- it does not;
.B SERVFAIL
\- a CNAME chain loops or runs longer than eight links;
.B REFUSED
\- the name is in none of the zones.
.TP
.I authoritative
Whether one of the server's zones holds the name.
.TP
.I zone
Which zone answered.
.TP
.I answers
The records, each with
.IR name ,
.IR type ,
.I ttl
and
.I value
in presentation form. A CNAME is followed while its target is in one of
the zones, and every link is listed.
.TP
.I authority
For a negative answer, the zone's SOA \- whose last field is how long a
resolver will cache that the name or type is not there.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The question was answered, whatever the answer was.
.TP
.B 1
No name was given, the type is unknown, or the request could not be
sent.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eds get-answer --name www.corp.example
euclid-cli eds get-answer --name corp.example --type MX
euclid-cli eds get-answer --name image-processing.app.euclid.internal
euclid-cli eds get-answer \e
    --name _http._tcp.image-processing.app.euclid.internal --type SRV
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eds (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eds-put-record (1),
.BR euclid-eds (8),
.BR dig (1)
